"3ecac406-0aef-584c-9d48-0a6c47d439e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186329167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186327266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329393 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7ec99a44-6d87-5ca7-8efa-c3acfffc845c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186329069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186329069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329486 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "acb9a9fe-ef3d-5f74-887c-394e168e90b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186468477 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186468478 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186468479 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42465" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has identical columns\n\nIII. $A$ has a zero column\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59d4edee-acd9-59e0-80f8-ec390e2e0ee0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329653 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186329654 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329654 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42467" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329654 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329654 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $3det(A)-4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186329654 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c45dadfd-a3b7-5456-a194-bb5508805b4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329654 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=7\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 4=-5.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-4det(B)=3\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 0=-15.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186329700 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329700 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42958" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329700 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329700 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $2det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186329700 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28b8a89e-dee6-5589-be7f-d0c7386a7fd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329700 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1)=5\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+3det(B)=2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0=10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452767 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452768 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452769 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- **II.** $A$ has two identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8066ca0-5e8f-5876-924e-8be55bf1f74e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392522 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "00ef10bc-f305-5726-8271-949923025e38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392523 #edb/ref 1080 "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392523 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392523 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ba7d7bc9-77ef-583c-8caa-22315aad7aca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392524 #edb/ref 1080 "$|B|$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392524 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392524 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23f02ed7-eb83-5988-a1ca-ee80eac659ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392525 #edb/ref 1080 "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392525 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392525 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d767aec8-a44c-5175-bbcd-b71f577015fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392526 #edb/ref 1080 "$|A|$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392526 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392526 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee7ae539-44fc-5d03-b8b9-5a5b498db62e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392527